+- **`exclusiveEnd()` — ONE definition.** End date on the 1st = exclusive (first-of-next-month billing); every other end date = inclusive last covered day. exclusiveEnd(): one definition, in the engine. The monthly split receives each bill's canonical end on its contribution and never converts an end date itself. A one-day period (start = end) covers that day, whatever the date; `canonicalPeriod` is the one place that says so. A delivery (T10b: a single delivery date, no billing period) has no period at all: it counts in full in the year it was delivered.
